request: Add a clear command that removes todos whose completed field is true.

governor turn 1: plan -> types, commands  (The Todo type has no 'completed' field. Its 'done' field is what the 'complete' command sets, so I read the request as removing todos where done is true. The types unit adds the clear variant to Command. The commands unit adds a clear() function, parses the 'clear' word in parseArgs, and handles it in run.)
round 1: owners types=ok commands=ok; oracle GREEN
governor turn 2: accept  (tsc and vitest both pass (18 tests, 0 failed). The manifest now shows the Command union with { kind: "clear" } and an exported clear(todos) in commands. Todo has no 'completed' field, so 'completed' was read as the existing done === true flag that the complete command sets. Clear keeps only todos with done === false and doesn't change their order or ids. parseArgs and run handle the new command, and run saves the result and reports how many were removed.)

